      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pine Bluffs is the easternmost incorporated community in Wyoming and sits along the Union Pacific Railroad line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pine_Bluffs,_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Rock Ranch, Pine Bluffs was renamed in 1868 for the distinctive pine trees covering nearby bluffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pine_Bluffs,_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Pine Bluffs consisted of basic structures, including a canvas-covered shed that served as a grocery, bakery, and saloon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pine_Bluffs,_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pine Bluffs Lighting Company was organized in 1909 to supply electrical power using innovative gas processes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Pine_Bluffs,_Wyoming"
    },
    {
